public static LinkedBuffer writeUTF8(final CharSequence str,final WriteSession session,final LinkedBuffer lb) {
    for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
        int ch = str.charAt(i);
        if (ch < 0x80) {
            lb.put((byte) ch);
        } else if (ch < 0xe0) {
            lb.put((byte) 0xC0 | (ch >> 6));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | (ch & 0x3F));
        } else if (ch < 0xf0) {
            lb.put((byte) 0xE0 | (ch >> 12));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | ((ch >> 6) & 0x3F));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | (ch & 0x3F));
        } else {
            lb.put((byte) 0xF0 | (ch >> 18));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | ((ch >> 12) & 0x3F));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | ((ch >> 6) & 0x3F));
            lb.put((byte) 0x80 | (ch & 0x3F));
        }
    }
    return lb;
}
```
This method takes a `CharSequence` representing a string, a `WriteSession`, and a `LinkedBuffer`. It converts each character in the string to its UTF-8 encoded byte representation and appends it to the `LinkedBuffer`. The method handles various Unicode character ranges and ensures that even multi-byte characters are properly encoded.

